 page='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>R339 — simpler black evidence and remaining 208 conflicts</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css"><header><h1>Three more supported pattern positions</h1><p>Your three corrections resolve positions 27 and 34. Three stable photographic corrections additionally resolve 92. The conditional 208 block now has <b>179 supported positions, 21 conflicts and eight insufficient positions</b>. Positions 112 and 196 have fewer disagreeing records but remain unresolved. No body, coordinate, link or winding changed.</p><p><a href="../../R339_REPORT.md">Report</a> · <a href="../../R339_REPRODUCE.md">Reproduce</a> · <a href="../verification.json">Independent checks</a> · <a href="ledger.html">All 29 unresolved positions with original pixels</a> · <a href="#solved">Solved cases and maker decisions</a> · <a href="#pattern">208 block</a></p><p>Please answer by <b>named photograph and its own feature number</b>. Each question target is feature 1 in its photograph and immediately matched diagram. Numbers in another photograph have a different key. Previously maker-reviewed bodies are not questions.</p></header><main><nav>BUTTONS</nav><div class="toolbar"><button id="previous">← Previous</button><button id="next">Next →</button><label><input id="numbers" type="checkbox" checked>Feature numbers</label><label><input id="links" type="checkbox">Photo links</label><label><input id="pixels" type="checkbox">Brightness samples</label><button id="zoom-in">Enlarge photos</button><button id="zoom-out">Reduce</button><button id="fit">Fit</button></div><p>Sample overlay: green retained material aperture, pink excluded bright pixels. These masks do not establish body identity or a physical center. All bead colors use the same geometry. Diagrams show current recorded colors and actual links, not predicted colors.</p>CARDS<section id="solved"><h2>Completed independent corrections — no questions</h2><p>NEW-1247-2991, NEW-2156-1135 and NEW-2235-1476 are corrected to black from independent native body evidence. The simple maximum-channel rule remains black at all three declared aperture sizes. The old rule abstained on all three. No pattern prediction selected their colors.</p>SOLVED<h2>Your exact R338 review decisions</h2><div class="scroll"><table><tr><th>Original named photograph</th><th>Own feature</th><th>Stable ID</th><th>Decision</th></tr>MAKER</table></div><p>Feature 12 in MAT25-K-2270-1942 is exactly NEW-2259-1961. All original R338 panels and keys are preserved. The completed R332-B-0098-0092 association is maker-confirmed and unchanged. <a href="../../r338/review/index.html">Historical R338 review</a>.</p></section><section id="method"><h2>A simpler conservative method</h2><p>Use one common neighbor-clipped aperture, exclude its brightest 20% by maximum RGB channel, and compare the remaining mean brightness with nearby black and colored references. A new correction must stay black under the predeclared smaller/larger apertures. Edge-near bodies and uncertain results keep their labels. No morphology, highlight-hue test, reflection tracking, annulus or pattern color is used.</p><p>A weighted-luminance trial was rejected because it mislabeled a visibly red body. Maximum-channel brightness removes that failure without extra per-bead rules. Both methods still abstain on many maker-confirmed black bodies. Control agreements are exposed retrospective checks, not new blind accuracy.</p></section><section id="pattern"><h2>Strict 208 block, conditional on current A mapping</h2><p>179 supported; 21 conflicting; eight insufficient. Unknowns are never filled by majority. N=2704 and 13 repetitions remain conditional; physical count and actual shortest complete sequence are unestablished.</p><div id="slots">SLOTS</div></section></main><script src="data.js"></script><script src="viewer.js"></script></html>'''
